  "summary": "Zombie Revenge is Sega's 1999 arcade brawler, followed by a Dreamcast version in Japan that November.",
  "body": [
    "Zombie Revenge is Sega's 1999 arcade brawler, followed by a Dreamcast version in Japan that November. Three AMS agents enter a city overrun by the undead, using guns, hand-to-hand attacks and found weapons to fight towards the source of the outbreak. The action brings the monsters close enough to punch and throw, turning the player from an aiming observer into a character moving through the crowd. One or two players can take part, sharing the task of controlling the dangerous space around them.",
    "Stick Breitling, Linda Rotta and Rikiya Busujima differ in their strengths and their proficiency with guns and close combat. Choosing a character changes how the next group is best approached, while weapons offer temporary alternatives. Boss encounters interrupt the advance through the city with larger threats. Switching between a firearm and a nearby opponent keeps distance relevant throughout the fighting: the safest target to shoot can cease to be the most urgent one when another zombie closes from the side.",
    "Developed by Sega AM1 and Data East, the game grew from the world of The House of the Dead and retains references to that series. Its arcade hardware was Sega's NAOMI, closely related to Dreamcast, which received the home conversion. That version also adds a one-on-one Battle Mode. Zombie Revenge carries the series' theatrical horror into another arcade tradition, using cooperative brawling and character movement to give familiar undead encounters a different pace and a more physical point of contact."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "The undead within arm’s reach",
    "Choose how to handle the next crowd",
    "Another route into the House of the Dead"
  ],
